        <briefdescription>
<para>Runs <computeroutput>body</computeroutput> on <computeroutput>worker</computeroutput>, answering the callback with 503 if the queue is full. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The callback is shared with the queued task so it remains valid for the busy reply; in that case <computeroutput>body</computeroutput> never executes. See <ref refid="boundedexecutor_8hpp_1af76f5db524067c26a058b1fee7e90e82" kindref="member">runOnExecutor()</ref> for the full contract. In everyday words: try to put this job on the password pool. If the queue is full, immediately answer the client with HTTP 503 (&quot;try
         again soon&quot;) instead of making them wait forever. <parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Body</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Callable invoked with a moved CALLBACK_ on a worker thread. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="inout">worker</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Pool that executes <computeroutput>body</computeroutput>. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="inout">callback</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Request callback moved into the task (or used for the 503 reply). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="inout">body</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Work to run on the password worker. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
