    <briefdescription>
<para>A dedicated thread pool for the slow work of hashing and checking passwords. (Originally: &quot;The pool for deliberately slow password work (hashing and verification), so it never runs on a Drogon IO thread.&quot;). </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This header declares a small class that is really just a named <ref refid="classBoundedExecutor" kindref="compound">BoundedExecutor</ref> for password jobs, plus a helper that submits a job to it. Password work is deliberately slow, so it must not run on the threads that handle web requests.</para>
<para>WHY THIS FILE MATTERS IN THE SERVER: Login and registration need password hashing, which is intentionally expensive. If that ran on a Drogon IO thread, one login would freeze request handling for everyone. <ref refid="controller_8hpp_1aa21c1eb0e46bd1813cc4cba55771c0a3" kindref="member">GateKeeper</ref> uses this pool to keep password work separate; without it the server would be slow and vulnerable to login-based denial of service.</para>
<para>CONCEPTS TO LEARN (for beginners):<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Thread pools: <ulink url="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thread_pool">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thread_pool</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>C++ threads: <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread/thread">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread/thread</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>HTTP 503 (server busy): <ulink url="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Status/503">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Status/503</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Perfect forwarding (std::forward): <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/forward">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/forward</ulink></para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><simplesect kind="author"><para>Amr Osman <ulink url="mailto:dr3mro@gmail.com">dr3mro@gmail.com</ulink> </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="date"><para>2026-11-16 </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
